  "question": {
    "text": "A balloon moving in a straight line passes vertically above two points <math><mi>A</mi></math> and <math><mi>B</mi></math> on a horizontal plane <math><mn>10</mn><mi></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></math> apart. When above <math><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;the balloon has an angle of elevation of <math><msup><mrow><mn>60</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></mrow></msup></math> as seen from <math><mi>B</mi></math>. When above <math><mi>B</mi></math> it has an angle of elevation of <math><msup><mrow><mn>45</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></mrow></msup></math> as seen from <math><mi>A</mi><mo>.</mo></math> The distance of <math><mi>B</mi></math> from the point <math><mi>C</mi></math> where it will touch the plane is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": true
